th SpA", "bbox": {"x": 873.0700569577263, "y": 1658.8957094561588, "width": 361.789814610635, "height": 30.577644035220146}}, {"kind": "text", "text": "we performed a family-based", "bbox": {"x": 1230.024193483902, "y": 1661.481249964792, "width": 315.50806451612897, "height": 27.462499999999903}}, {"kind": "text", "text": "To identify whether one or several loci of the refined SPA2", "bbox": {"x": 896.2258050988911, "y": 1629.4416666094533, "width": 649.3064516129032, "height": 27.462499999999903}}, {"kind": "text", "text": "between markers D9S279 and D9S112 comprising both signifidecided to continue our investigations on the 13.1 Mb region characterize linkage localization with high precision [27], we", "bbox": {"x": 873.1013893711138, "y": 1513.3407993531348, "width": 672.4877246733635, "height": 90.31164012352617}}, {"kind": "text", "text": "SpA. Since non parametric linkage analyses usually do not", "bbox": {"x": 873.36290065373, "y": 1482.974999885573, "width": 672.1693548387096, "height": 27.462500000000148}}, {"kind": "text", "text": "[12], supporting the validity of linkage between this region and suggestive linkage peak reported in AS (D9S1682, P=6x10\")", "bbox": {"x": 868.7903223551699, "y": 1428.0499999862316, "width": 672.1693548387096, "height": 54.92500000000005}}, {"kind": "text", "text": "screen. The second statistically significant area was located near a D9S1776, which corresponded to the linkage peak in our former", "bbox": {"x": 868.6869825261903, "y": 1361.635002884452, "width": 677.1036686435822, "height": 61.96511992911499}}, {"kind": "text", "text": "(115.9 Mb) from the p-telomere,", "bbox": {"x": 873.362902841515, "y": 1336.508333304118, "width": 370.37903225806457, "height": 27.462500000000148}}, {"kind": "text", "text": "only 1,5 col apart trom", "bbox": {"x": 1257.4596772376242, "y": 1345.662499982396, "width": 278.92741935483866, "height": 13.731249999999951}}, {"kind": "text", "text": "highest linkage peak located on the marker D9S1824 at 120.1 cM", "bbox": {"x": 873.3629029956114, "y": 1309.0458333239285, "width": 672.1693548387096, "height": 27.462500000000148}}, {"kind": "text", "text": "revealed two areas of statistically signilicant linkage, with the", "bbox": {"x": 873.3629030040022, "y": 1281.583333323086, "width": 667.5967741935484, "height": 27.462499999999903}}, {"kind": "text", "text": "microsatellite markers in an extended set of famil", "bbox": {"x": 873.3628993391129, "y": 1249.5437496567188, "width": 512.1290322580646, "height": 27.462500000000148}}, {"kind": "text", "text": "our first attempt was to refine it using a fine-grained set of 28", "bbox": {"x": 873.362903010827, "y": 1222.0812499897527, "width": 667.5967741935484, "height": 27.462499999999903}}, {"kind": "text", "text": "linkage in this locus was spread over a long distance of 23.95 cM,", "bbox": {"x": 873.3629029956005, "y": 1194.6187499921082, "width": 667.5967741935484, "height": 22.885416666666828}}, {"kind": "text", "text": "SpA on chromosome 9q31-34 called SPA2", "bbox": {"x": 873.3629029882117, "y": 1162.5791666532045, "width": 484.6935483870967, "height": 27.462500000000148}}, {"kind": "text", "text": "previous whole genome linkage screen the susceptibility region for The basis of our investigations aimed to narrow down from our", "bbox": {"x": 868.7903223621773, "y": 1107.654166657004, "width": 672.1693548387096, "height": 54.92500000000005}}, {"kind": "text", "text": "and association steps.", "bbox": {"x": 873.3629028638104, "y": 1075.6145832761197, "width": 228.6290322580645, "height": 27.462499999999903}}, {"kind": "text", "text": "This was achieved by a comprehensive study with several linkage determining a haplotype near the 7MFSF15 gene (9q32) and SpA.", "bbox": {"x": 868.5792478844523, "y": 1013.6206010732203, "width": 672.6675272295552, "height": 62.028007158636946}}, {"kind": "text", "text": "We report for the first time an association between several SNPS", "bbox": {"x": 896.225806222984, "y": 988.6499999902616, "width": 644.733870967742, "height": 27.462500000000148}}, {"kind": "text", "text": "as well as in the case/control one [P= 7.0x10-* at 3 df.", "bbox": {"x": 868.6442815267042, "y": 870.1593122314121, "width": 594.8319983943813, "height": 36.2496448000272}}, {"kind": "text", "text": "family-based sample (P= 4.5x10", "bbox": {"x": 873.3628974338711, "y": 846.7604162089584, "width": 347.5161290322581, "height": 27.462499999999903}}, {"kind": "text", "text": "> at 4 degrees-of-freedom (d),", "bbox": {"x": 1220.458127090057, "y": 846.4788166806634, "width": 325.42364871117377, "height": 32.672102625171505}}, {"kind": "text", "text": "A significant omnibus haplotype association was detected in", "bbox": {"x": 896.2258062162595, "y": 819.2979166565702, "width": 649.3064516129032, "height": 27.462499999999903}}, {"kind": "text", "text": "Table S5).", "bbox": {"x": 873.214423456233, "y": 786.6512152209019, "width": 110.03889402266472, "height": 28.676735986272558}}, {"kind": "text", "text": "patients, independently of the presence of HLA-B27 (Table S4 and that the frequency of II2 haplotype was significantly decreased in controls. Case/control HLA-B27 conditioned analyses showed all the other haplotypes being more frequent in cases than in frequent in controls than in cases (Table 4; P= 8.75x10 *, with showed that the rare haplotype H2 was very significantly more", "bbox": {"x": 868.7903221716061, "y": 613.3291666485829, "width": 676.741935483871, "height": 173.9291666666668}}, {"kind": "text", "text": "The case/control haplotype association analysis conversely", "bbox": {"x": 896.2258062197177, "y": 585.8666666568587, "width": 649.3064516129032, "height": 27.462499999999903}}, {"kind": "text", "text": "with Bonferroni method was set to 0.013.", "bbox": {"x": 873.3629030076893, "y": 553.8270833201807, "width": 425.25, "height": 22.885416666666828}}, {"kind": "text", "text": "corrected for the multiplicity of tested haplotypes and extrapolated three alleles being undertransmitted. The signilicance threshold with a high significance level (Table 4; P= 8.81 × 10-*), the other most frequent allele III as overtransmitted to affected children", "bbox": {"x": 868.7903239984706, "y": 439.3999998524922, "width": 676.741935483871, "height": 114.42708333333317}}, {"kind": "text", "text": "The family-based haplotype association analysis identified the", "bbox": {"x": 896.2258057301613, "y": 407.36041663615276, "width": 649.3064516129034, "height": 27.462499999999903}}, {"kind": "text", "text": "frequencies.", "bbox": {"x": 868.790322302314, "y": 379.8979166169157, "width": 128.0322580645162, "height": 22.885416666666586}}, {"kind": "text", "text": "are displayed in the Table 4, together with their estimated Association results for the haplotypes comprising these six SNPS", "bbox": {"x": 868.7903223520159, "y": 320.3958333245454, "width": 676.741935483871, "height": 54.92500000000005}}, {"kind": "text", "text": "haplotype test may be more powerful to detect association. known that in the presence of multiple tightly linked markers a analysis were located in the same strong LD block (Figure 4). It is", "bbox": {"x": 868.7903223192138, "y": 233.43124999068255, "width": 676.7419354838711, "height": 82.38749999999995}}, {"kind": "text", "text": "The six SNPs presenting the lowest P-values alter the combined", "bbox": {"x": 896.0442004176626, "y": 200.55291071140755, "width": 649.640450385309, "height": 32.64886529843014}}, {"kind": "text", "text": "Family-based and case/control haplotypic analyses", "bbox": {"x": 873.0776798767315, "y": 167.15913600889493, "width": 604.0613047692083, "height": 35.900085303187176}}, {"kind": "text", "text": "Mapping a SpA Locus Near to TNFSF15", "bbox": {"x": 1166.0080642902883, "y": 82.38749998325463, "width": 379.52419354838713, "height": 27.462499999999903}}], "ms": 677.502625}